H2800.definition:
the same as H2799 (חֲרֹשֶׁת);
Charosheth, a place in Palestine
KJV: Harosheth.

H2801.definition:
a primitive root;
to engrave
KJV: graven.

H2802.definition:
from H2801 (חָרַת) (but equivalent to H2793 (חֹרֶשׁ)); forest;
Chereth, a thicket in Palestine
KJV: Hereth.

H2803.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to plait or interpenetrate, i.e. (literally) to weave or (generally) to fabricate; figuratively, to plot or contrive (usually in a malicious sense); hence (from the mental effort) to think, regard, value, compute
KJV: (make) account (of), conceive, consider, count, cunning (man, work, workman), devise, esteem, find out, forecast, hold, imagine, impute, invent, be like, mean, purpose, reckon(-ing be made), regard, think.

H2804.definition:
(Aramaic) corresponding to H2803 (חָשַׁב);
to regard
KJV: repute.

H2805.definition:
from H2803 (חָשַׁב);
a belt or strap (as being interlaced)
KJV: curious girdle.

H2806.definition:
from H2803 (חָשַׁב) and H1777 (דִּין); considerate judge;
Chasbaddanah, an Israelite
KJV: Hasbadana.

H2807.definition:
from H2803 (חָשַׁב); estimation;
Cashubah, an Israelite
KJV: Hashubah.

H2808.definition:
from H2803 (חָשַׁב);
properly, contrivance; by implication, intelligence
KJV: account, device, reason.

H2809.definition:
the same as H2808 (חֶשְׁבּוֹן);
Cheshbon, a place East of the Jordan
KJV: Heshbon.

H2810.definition:
from H2803 (חָשַׁב);
a contrivance, i.e. actual (a warlike machine) or mental (a machination)
KJV: engine, invention.

H2811.definition:
or חֲשַׁבְיָהוּ; from H2803 (חָשַׁב) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has regarded;
Chashabjah, the name of nine Israelites
KJV: Hashabiah.

H2812.definition:
feminine of H2808 (חֶשְׁבּוֹן); inventiveness;
Chashnah, an Israelite
KJV: Hashabnah.

H2813.definition:
from H2808 (חֶשְׁבּוֹן) and H3050 (יָהּ); thought of Jah;
Chashabnejah, the name of two Israelites
KJV: Hashabniah.

H2814.definition:
a primitive root;
to hush or keep quiet
KJV: hold peace, keep silence, be silent, (be) still.

H2815.definition:
from H2803 (חָשַׁב); intelligent;
Chashshub, the name of two or three Israelites
KJV: Hashub, Hasshub.

H2816.definition:
(Aramaic) from a root corresponding to H2821 (חָשַׁךְ);
the dark
KJV: darkness.

H2817.definition:
or חֲשֻׂפָא; from H2834 (חָשַׂף); nakedness;
Chasupha, one of the Nethinim
KJV: Hashupha, Hasupha.

H2818.definition:
(Aramaic) a collateral root to one corresponding to H2363 (חוּשׁ) in the sense of readiness;
to be necessary (from the idea of convenience) or (transitively) to need
KJV: careful, have need of.

H2819.definition:
from a root corresponding to H2818 (חֲשַׁח);
necessity
KJV: be needful.

H2821.definition:
a primitive root;
to be dark (as withholding light); transitively, to darken
KJV: be black, be (make) dark, darken, cause darkness, be dim, hide.

H2822.definition:
from H2821 (חָשַׁךְ);
the dark; hence (literally) darkness; figuratively, misery, destruction, death, ignorance, sorrow, wickedness
KJV: dark(-ness), night, obscurity.

H2823.definition:
from H2821 (חָשַׁךְ);
dark (figuratively, i.e. obscure)
KJV: meaning

H2825.definition:
or חֲשֵׁיכָהxlit chăshêkâh corrected to chăshêykâh; from H2821 (חָשַׁךְ);
darkness; figuratively, misery
KJV: darkness.

H2826.definition:
a primitive root;
to make (intrans. be) unsteady, i.e. weak
KJV: feeble.

H2827.definition:
(Aramaic) a root corresponding to H2826 (חָשַׁל);
to weaken, i.e. crush
KJV: subdue.

H2828.definition:
from the same as H2831 (חַשְׁמַן); enriched;
Chashum, the name of two or three Israelites
KJV: Hashum.

H2829.definition:
the same as H2831 (חַשְׁמַן); opulent;
Cheshmon, a place in Palestine
KJV: Heshmon.

H2830.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
probably bronze or polished spectrum metal
KJV: amber.

H2832.definition:
feminine of H2831 (חַשְׁמַן); fertile;
Chasmonah, a place in the Desert
KJV: Hashmonah.

H2833.definition:
from an unused root probably meaning to contain or sparkle;
perhaps a pocket (as holding the Urim and Thummim), or rich (as containing gems), used only of the gorget of the highpriest
KJV: breastplate.

H2834.definition:
a primitive root;
to strip off, i.e. generally to make naked (for exertion or in disgrace), to drain away or bail up (a liquid)
KJV: make bare, clean, discover, draw out, take, uncover.

H2835.definition:
from H2834 (חָשַׂף);
properly, drawn off, i.e. separated; hence, a small company (as divided from the rest)
KJV: little flock.

H2837.definition:
from H2836 (חָשַׁק);
delight
KJV: desire, pleasure.

H2838.definition:
or חָשׁוּק; past participle of H2836 (חָשַׁק);
attached, i.e. a fence-rail or rod connecting the posts or pillars
KJV: fillet.

H2839.definition:
from H2836 (חָשַׁק);
conjoined, i.e. a wheel-spoke or rod connecting the hub with the rim
KJV: felloe.

H2840.definition:
from an unused root meaning to bind together;
combined, i.e. the nave or hub of awheel (as holding the spokes together)
KJV: spoke.

H2841.definition:
from the same as H2840 (חִשֻּׁר);
properly, a combination or gathering, i.e. of watery clouds
KJV: dark.

H2842.definition:
by variation for H7179 (קַשׁ);
dry grass
KJV: chaff.

H2843.definition:
patronymically from H2364 (חוּשָׁה);
a Chushathite or descendant of Chushah
KJV: Hushathite.

H2844.definition:
from H2865 (חָתַת);
concretely, crushed; also afraid; abstractly, terror
KJV: broken, dismayed, dread, fear.

H2845.definition:
from H2865 (חָתַת); terror;
Cheth, an aboriginal Canaanite
KJV: Heth.

H2846.definition:
a primitive root;
to lay hold of; especially to pick up fire
KJV: heap, take (away).

H2848.definition:
from H2853 (חָתַל);
swathed, i.e. a bandage
KJV: roller.

H2850.definition:
patronymically from H2845 (חֵת);
a Chittite, or descendant of Cheth
KJV: Hittite, Hittities.

H2852.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to cut off, i.e. (figuratively) to decree
KJV: determine.

H2853.definition:
a primitive root;
to swathe
KJV: [idiom] at all, swaddle.

H2854.definition:
from H2853 (חָתַל);
a swathing cloth (figuratively)
KJV: swaddling band.

H2855.definition:
from H2853 (חָתַל); enswathed;
Chethlon, a place in Palestine
KJV: Hethlon.

H2856.definition:
a primitive root;
to close up; especially to seal
KJV: make an end, mark, seal (up), stop.

H2857.definition:
(Aramaic) a root corresponding to H2856 (חָתַם);
to seal
KJV: seal.

H2858.definition:
feminine active participle of H2856 (חָתַם);
a seal
KJV: signet.

H2859.definition:
a primitive root;
to give (a daughter) away in marriage; hence (generally) to contract affinity by marriage
KJV: join in affinity, father in law, make marriages, mother in law, son in law.

H2860.definition:
from H2859 (חָתַן);
a relative by marriage (especially through the bride); figuratively, a circumcised child (as a species of religious espousal)
KJV: bridegroom, husband, son in law.

H2861.definition:
from H2859 (חָתַן);
a wedding
KJV: espousal.

H2862.definition:
a primitive root;
to clutch
KJV: take away.

H2863.definition:
from H2862 (חָתַף);
properly, rapine; figuratively, robbery
KJV: prey.

H2864.definition:
a primitive root;
to force a passage, as by burglary; figuratively, with oars
KJV: dig (through), row.

H2865.definition:
a primitive root;
properly, to prostrate; hence, to break down, either (literally) by violence, or (figuratively) by confusion and fear
KJV: abolish, affright, be (make) afraid, amaze, beat down, discourage, (cause to) dismay, go down, scare, terrify.

H2866.definition:
from H2865 (חָתַת);
dismay
KJV: casting down.

H2867.definition:
the same as H2866 (חֲתַת);
Chathath, an Israelite
KJV: cathath. f

H2868.definition:
a primitive root;
to rejoice
KJV: be glad

H2869.definition:
the same as H2896 (טוֹב);
good
KJV: fine, good.

H2870.definition:
from H2895 (טוֹב) and H410 (אֵל); pleasing (to) God;
Tabeel, the name of a Syrian and of a Persian
KJV: Tabeal, Tabeel.

H2871.definition:
passive participle of H2881 (טָבַל);
properly, dyed, i.e. a turban (probably as of colored stuff)
KJV: dyed attire.

H2872.definition:
from an unused root meaning to pile up;
properly, accumulated; i.e. (by implication) a summit
KJV: middle, midst.

H2873.definition:
a primitive root;
to slaughter (animals or men)
KJV: kill, (make) slaughter, slay.

H2874.definition:
from H2873 (טָבַח);
properly, something slaughtered; hence, a beast (or meat, as butchered); abstractly butchery (or concretely, a place of slaughter)
KJV: [idiom] beast, slaughter, [idiom] slay, [idiom] sore.

H2875.definition:
the same as H2874 (טֶבַח); massacre;
Tebach, the name of a Mesopotamian and of an Israelite
KJV: Tebah.

H2876.definition:
from H2873 (טָבַח);
properly, a butcher; hence, a lifeguardsman (because he was acting as an executioner); also a cook (usually slaughtering the animal for food)
KJV: cook, guard.

H2877.definition:
(Aramaic) the same as H2876 (טַבָּח);
a lifeguardsman
KJV: guard.

H2878.definition:
feminine of H2874 (טֶבַח) and meaning the same
{properly, something slaughtered; hence, a beast (or meat, as butchered); abstractly butchery (or concretely, a place of slaughter)}
KJV: flesh, slaughter.

H2879.definition:
feminine of H2876 (טַבָּח);
a female cook
KJV: cook.

H2880.definition:
from H2878 (טִבְחָה); slaughter;
Tibchath, a place in Syria
KJV: Tibhath.

H2881.definition:
a primitive root;
to dip, to immerse
KJV: dip, plunge.

H2882.definition:
from H2881 (טָבַל) and H3050 (יָהּ); Jah has dipped;
Tebaljah, an Israelite
KJV: Tebaliah.

H2883.definition:
a primitive root;
to sink
KJV: drown, fasten, settle, sink.

H2884.definition:
plural of H2885 (טַבַּעַת); rings;
Tabbaoth, one of the Nethinim
KJV: Tabaoth.

H2885.definition:
from H2883 (טָבַע);
properly, a seal (as sunk into the wax), i.e. signet (for sealing); hence (generally) a ring of any kind
KJV: ring.

H2886.definition:
from H2895 (טוֹב) and H7417 (רִמּוֹן); pleasing (to) Rimmon;
Tabrimmon, a Syrian
KJV: Tabrimmon.

H2887.definition:
probably of foreign derivation;
Tebeth, the tenth Hebrew month
KJV: Tebeth.

H2888.definition:
of uncertain derivation;
Tabbath, a place East of the Jordan
KJV: Tabbath.

H2889.definition:
or טָהֹר; from H2891 (טָהֵר);
pure (in a physical, chemical, ceremonial or moral sense)
KJV: clean, fair, pure(-ness).

H2892.definition:
from H2891 (טָהֵר);
literally brightness; ceremonially purification
KJV: clearness, glory, purifying.

H2893.definition:
feminine of H2892 (טֹהַר);
ceremonial purification; moral purity
KJV: [idiom] is cleansed, cleansing, purification(-fying).

H2894.definition:
a primitive root;
to sweep away
KJV: sweep.

H2896.definition:
from H2895 (טוֹב);
good (as an adjective) in the widest sense; used likewise as a noun, both in the masculine and the feminine, the singular and the plural (good, a good or good thing, a good man or woman; the good, goods or good things, good men or women), also as an adverb (well)
KJV: beautiful, best, better, bountiful, cheerful, at ease, [idiom] fair (word), (be in) favour, fine, glad, good (deed, -lier, -liest, -ly, -ness, -s), graciously, joyful, kindly, kindness, liketh (best), loving, merry, [idiom] most, pleasant, [phrase] pleaseth, pleasure, precious, prosperity, ready, sweet, wealth, welfare, (be) well(-favoured).

H2897.definition:
the same as H2896 (טוֹב); good;
Tob, a region apparently East of the Jordan
KJV: Tob.

H2898.definition:
from H2895 (טוֹב);
good (as a noun), in the widest sense, especially goodness (superlative concretely, the best), beauty, gladness, welfare
KJV: fair, gladness, good(-ness, thing, -s), joy, go well with.

H2899.definition:
from H2896 (טוֹב) and H138 (אֲדֹנִיָּה); pleasing (to) Adonijah;
Tob-Adonijah, an Israelite
KJV: Tob-adonijah.
